WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:10.660
Close your eyes. A vibrator on your biceps tendon, at 100 Hz, can make you misjudge

2
00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:11.660
where your elbow is.

3
00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:13.540
The joint has not moved.

4
00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:20.280
In one classic experiment on human subjects, the error reached as much as 40 degrees

5
00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:21.700
while the muscle contracted.

6
00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:29.560
So your sense of limb position is a computed estimate, built from sensors you cannot feel.

8
00:00:29.833 --> 00:00:34.773
Position is read from populations of afferents, not from one receptor.

9
00:00:35.793 --> 00:00:36.853
Take the muscle spindle.

10
00:00:37.453 --> 00:00:43.413
It has two sensory endings, a primary ending called Ia, and a secondary ending

11
00:00:43.533 --> 00:00:47.273
called type II. Both signal static muscle length.

12
00:00:48.353 --> 00:00:51.613
Ia endings are also more sensitive to the rate of change.

13
00:00:52.233 --> 00:00:57.713
So the old rule, that Ia is velocity and type II is position, is wrong.

14
00:00:58.467 --> 00:01:02.587
Human recordings separate the two classes by vibration.

15
00:01:03.407 --> 00:01:09.407
In the leg of healthy people, one study recorded 15 primary and 5 secondary endings.

16
00:01:10.087 --> 00:01:14.327
The secondary endings were less sensitive to low-amplitude tendon vibration.

17
00:01:14.687 --> 00:01:18.267
So primary endings are the likely carriers of the illusion.

18
00:01:18.947 --> 00:01:21.987
But the experiments do not show that only they act.

19
00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:27.500
Which protein turns stretch into current at a spindle ending?

20
00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:30.280
A channel called Piezo2.

21
00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:33.820
In mouse, three kinds of evidence were gathered.

22
00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:36.020
First, where it is.

23
00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:40.160
A reporter showed it in endings on spindles and tendon organs.

24
00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:42.940
Second, what current it carries.

25
00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:47.400
Dissociated sensory neurons gave rapidly adapting currents.

26
00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:50.440
Third, whether the ending needs it.

27
00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:53.840
Deleting it sharply reduced stretch-evoked firing.

28
00:01:54.750 --> 00:02:01.370
In mouse cell bodies in culture, 23 of 25 labelled neurons had rapidly adapting

29
00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:05.730
currents. The label marks proprioceptors and some other neurons.

30
00:02:06.590 --> 00:02:10.230
The inactivation time constant was 5.6 milliseconds.

31
00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:12.710
Assume one exponential decay.

32
00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:15.590
That is our assumption, not the paper's.

33
00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:21.210
About 17% is left at 10 milliseconds and about 3% at 20.

34
00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:27.780
A small stretch response remained after deletion, in one of eight muscles for each

35
00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:33.320
mouse line. So Piezo2 is the principal transducer, not the only one.

36
00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:39.860
In humans, two people with inactivating PIEZO2 variants were markedly worse at

37
00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:42.940
reaching and joint angle tasks without visual cues.

38
00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:45.540
Two people are a clinical series.

39
00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:50.420
Keep this rule. Limb position is an estimate from many signals.
